        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.1,
            0.884,
            0.155
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) The volume of a solid can be measured by the method of displacement, where the solid is in water and the in water level is measured."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.294,
            0.156,
            0.883,
            0.209
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) The maximum amount of dissolved in at a particular temperature is called solubility at that temperature."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.29,
            0.209,
            0.882,
            0.245
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Generally, the density with increase in temperature."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.291,
            0.245,
            0.883,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) The solution in which glucose has completely dissolved in water, and no more glucose can dissolve at a given temperature, is called a solution of glucose."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.301,
            0.882,
            0.337
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. You pour oil into a glass containing some water. The oil floats on top. What does this tell you?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.339,
            0.577,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Oil is denser than water"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.296,
            0.358,
            0.576,
            0.375
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Water is denser than oil"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.29,
            0.375,
            0.696,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Oil and water have the same density"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.291,
            0.394,
            0.553,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) Oil dissolves in water"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.413,
            0.883,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. A stone sculpture weighs 225 g and has a volume of 90 cm"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Calculate its density and predict whether it will float or sink in water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.469,
            0.882,
            0.507
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Which one of the following is the most appropriate statement, and why are the other statements not appropriate?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.508,
            0.882,
            0.544
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) A saturated solution can still dissolve more solute at a given temperature."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.294,
            0.543,
            0.882,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) An unsaturated solution has dissolved the maximum amount of solute possible at a given temperature."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.29,
            0.58,
            0.882,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) No more solute can be dissolved into the saturated solution at that temperature."
